## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical end-to-end security for data integration pipelines, including artifact signing, attestation storage, and runtime enforcement with policy engines.

## Key Concepts

- Artifact signing with cosign and key management
- Attestations stored in Rekor registry
- Policy-driven runtime enforcement (Kyverno/OPA)
- Integration points with Kafka Connect

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal illustration: pseudo-check attestation reference in manifest
async function isAttested(manifest) {
  const ref = manifest.attestationRef;
  // fetch and verify against Rekor/public cosign key
  return !!ref;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle rotation of signing keys and revocation?
- What metrics and alerts would you add to detect failed attestations at startup?

## Why This Is Asked
Addresses multi-cloud data governance, tenancy, and compliance through policy-as-code, ensuring data privacy, residency, and auditable CI validation in production-scale ML platforms.

## Key Concepts
- Data masking in logs/telemetry
- Per-tenant data residency and envelope encryption
- Tenant-aware RBAC across clouds
- Policy-as-code (OPA/Kyverno) + CI gates

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactPII(logEntry) {
  const redacted = { ...logEntry };
  for (const k of Object.keys(redacted)) {
    if (k.toLowerCase().includes('ssn') || k.toLowerCase().includes('email')) {
      redacted[k] = 'REDACTED';
    }
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test fail-closed masking in CI across multiple tenants?
- What metrics would you surface to detect residency violations at runtime?
